hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27958","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Habibah bint Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, from her mother Umm Habibah, from Zaynab, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Sufyan said: four women, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, awoke from sleep with his face red, saying: There is no god but Allah; woe to the Arabs from an evil drawing near; there was opened today of the barrier of Yajuj and Majuj like this, and he made a circle. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perish while the righteous are among us. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes, when filth increases."
"27959","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Salih, meaning Ibn Kaysan, Ibn Shihab said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed, from Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her in fright, saying: There is no god but Allah; woe to the Arabs from an evil drawing near; there was opened today of the barrier of Yajuj and Majuj like this. He said: And he made a circle with his two fingers, the thumb and the one next to it. Zaynab bint Jahsh said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perish while the righteous are among us. He said: Yes, when filth increases."
"27960","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Abu al-Jarrah, the freedman of Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Umm Habibah, that she narrated to him, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would command them with the tooth-stick at every prayer, as they perform ablution."
"27961","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Ibn Shihab mentioned, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me, holding with his two fingers, the forefinger with the thumb, saying: Woe to the Arabs from an evil drawing near; there was opened today of the barrier of Yajuj and Majuj like the place of the dirham. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perish while the righteous are among us. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes, when filth increases."
